Public Health</source><year>2005</year><volume>96</volume><fpage>308</fpage><lpage>312</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16625804</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Calzavara</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Burchell</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Schlossberg</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Myers</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Wallace</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Millson</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Major</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Escobar</surname><given-names>MA</given-names></name></person-group><source>omparison of HIV testing behaviours reported by Aboriginals and non-Aboriginal inmates: Implications for HIV testing programs</source><year>1998</year><publisher-name>Paper presented at the VIIth Annual Conference on HIV/AIDS Research; Quebec City, Canada</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stokes</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Pennock</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Archibald</surname><given-names>CP</given-names></name></person-group><source>Factors associated with late HIV diagnosis in Canada, 1996&#x02013;2005</source><year>2006</year><publisher-name>XVI International Conference on AIDS; August 13&#x02013;18 Toronto, Canada</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Goldstone</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name><name><surname>Albert</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Churchill</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Schilder</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surnam